# Replacement rotated-pentagon chapter

`chapter.tex` is the integration-ready chapter. `standalone.tex` provides its
own preamble and bibliography; `build-revised/standalone.pdf` is the five-page review
copy, including references. The main thesis has not been edited.

Build from this directory:

```sh
latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error -outdir=build-revised standalone.tex
```

The local figure is copied unchanged from
`thesis/working/rotated-regular-polygons/lagrangian-products-5x5.png`.
The two entries in `references.bib` use the same keys and publication metadata
as `thesis/bibliography.bib`; no new bibliography entries are needed when
integrating into the thesis.

## Integration

For the recovered candidate thesis, follow `docs/sprint-two/integration.md`:
add the replacement under `thesis/candidate/` and replace the input of
`recovered/thesis-candidate/09-pentagon.tex`.
For the original thesis, replace the input of `09-rotated-regular-polygons`.
Do not also input the old empirical/theorem/certificate files: this chapter
contains the full replacement and preserves the principal section, theorem,
and figure labels.

For a build whose working directory is `thesis/`, the replacement input is:

```tex
\providecommand{\pentagonassetpath}{../docs/pentagon-chapter/assets/}
\input{../docs/pentagon-chapter/chapter.tex}
```

When building from the repository root, use
`\input{docs/pentagon-chapter/chapter.tex}`; the asset path defaults accordingly.
The thesis already supplies `amsmath`, `amssymb`, `amsthm`, `graphicx`,
`biblatex`, and the `theorem` environment. Do not input the
standalone wrapper or its bibliography into the thesis.

The candidate main file also has a separate appendix titled “Pentagon
computation: source and exploratory plots”, with `pentagon-source.tex` and
`pentagon-diagnostics.tex` inputs. To deliver a thesis without the old
computational proof, omit that appendix block as well. Its files can remain
in the repository as historical material. Two candidate overview passages
also need updating at integration: `01-introduction.tex` currently says
“An exhaustive comparison proves the formula”; replace this with
“Positive interpolation of the known endpoint capacity, together with an
explicit attaining candidate, proves the formula.” In `14-conclusion.tex`,
replace “An exhaustive exact calculation then proves the separate theorem”
with “An analytic interpolation argument then proves the separate theorem”.
The corresponding overview prose in the original thesis also describes
exact computation and should be aligned if that version is the integration
target. Check the table of contents after integration; no full-thesis
integration build has been performed here.

## Scope and provenance

The chapter retains the circumradius-one normalization and the existing
explicit six-facet candidate. It proves the full rotation profile by a common
feasible set, first harmonics, and positive interpolation of the independently
known Haim–Kislev–Ostrover endpoint capacity. Its scope is the empirical
motivation, capacity and systolic profile, family maximum, and analytic proof.
The proof does not use the former enumeration certificate.

The endpoint interpolation came from section 2 of the September 2026
AI-assisted thesis review; the chapter
acknowledges that provenance in a footnote. The historical thesis files supply
the numerical plot and explicit word. Scholarly inputs are cited to the
published Haim–Kislev and Haim–Kislev–Ostrover papers, not to the review.

The standalone document was compiled with resolved references and citations,
and every page was visually inspected. Separate fresh-context mathematical
and sequential-reader reviews found no material defects. These checks accept
the published capacity theorems as inputs and do not independently reproduce
the historical floating-point samples. No mathematical issue is currently
unresolved.
